From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] doskey, conhost: doskey.exe, and the console host expands doskey macros (9262)

Windows has doskey.exe in system32; Wine had none. Git for Windows' Git CMD
(git-cmd.exe, what SG Store's Open starts for Git) runs
  cmd.exe /K "C:\windows\system32\doskey.exe git=^"C:\Program Files\Git\cmd\git.exe^" $*"
and so opened with "Can't recognize 'C:\windows\system32\doskey.exe
git=...' as an internal or external command" (found in apps11's walk).

doskey.exe, as Windows': name=text defines a macro in the console's alias
table for a program (AddConsoleAlias; cmd.exe unless /EXENAME= names
another; the text kept as typed), name= removes it, /MACROS[:ALL|:exe]
lists them, /HISTORY the command history (9705), /MACROFILE= loads a file
of name=text lines ([exe] headers), /LISTSIZE= sets the history size,
/REINSTALL /INSERT /OVERSTRIKE are accepted, /? shows the usage.

conhost: a macro typed at the start of a line the reading program reads
(its input exe name, 9705) is expanded from that program's aliases (5623):
$1-$9 the words after the name, $* all of them, $T separates commands
(each read as a line of its own), $G $L $B $$ are > < | $. The history
keeps the line as typed.

Gate: make test-doskey (a real console on its own Xvfb). Mutants:
SG_MUTANT_MACRO_NO_EXPAND, SG_MUTANT_DOSKEY_NO_ALIAS.
